    "body": "also noticed my directory truncation module works, so it seems just aws module is broken and my creds are aws sso.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, when I changed my was profile to personal (Which uses regular aws credentials methods)\r\n\r\n*BINGO* aws module is back:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/388653/157424447-2ba58426-4441-421d-bf22-ca0ef325b436.png)\r\n\r\n\r\nSO it seems your 1.3.0 -> 1.4.0 migration broke aws profiles that use sso login. hope that helps (cant give more config details as I might be breaking my confidentiality) but hope that is useful.\r\n\r\nwhat I can share is that this is the contents of my usual was profile:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n[profile development]\r\nsso_start_url = https://<endpointURL>\r\nsso_region = <SSO-Default-Region>\r\nsso_account_id = <AWS ACCOUNT ID>\r\nsso_role_name = <AWS-ROLE-NAME>\r\nregion = <AWS-REGION - (COULD BE DIFFERENT FROM SSO REGION>\r\n\r\n```\r\nEverything between < > is obviously redacted",
    "author_association": "NONE",
